{"entryId":"3179","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3179:1","sourceSha256":"2653e1832660588dc76952d17133dc681206793430b798a00d36c7852df39f78","englishSha256":"9670f23595960ae3b6e16f21ae059c2901f484bac8148d7f4ca9d5da763c2371","citations":[{"id":"3179:1:link-001","he":[12,26],"en":[20,41],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_21a.11"},"reference":"Shabbat 21a:11","assessment":"Shabbat gives Rabbah bar Mattana as reciter of a baraita.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 21a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_21a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3179:1:link-002","he":[28,127],"en":[42,312],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_14a.5"},"reference":"Horayot 14a:5","assessment":"The Bavli first puts the four scholars together to choose a head. The inquiry about comparative merit follows and spells the name out as bar Rav Mattana. The original unresolved answer is explicit.","evidence":[{"reference":"Horayot 14a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_14a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Horayot 14a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_14a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3179:1:link-003","he":[128,159],"en":[313,477],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_34a.2"},"reference":"Pesachim 34a:2","assessment":"The direct Pesahim locus has Abaye bar Avin and Rav Hananya bar Avin study Terumot in Rabbah’s academy. The scholar who approaches is spelled Rava bar Mattana there.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 34a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_34a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 137:1","target":{"entry":137,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Horayot distinguishes the choice of a head from the later unresolved comparison. Pesahim places the sons of Avin in Rabbah’s academy and names Rava bar Mattana as their interlocutor.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Horayot 14a:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_14a.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Horayot 14a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Horayot_14a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 34a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_34a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 137:1","target":{"entry":137,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
